Subject: [PATCH 2/3] incusd: Re-introduce core scheduling detection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Depending on environment, even recent kernels will fail to set up core
scheduling, so we need to keep detecting it.

Closes #3304

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
